  "slug": "optimization-framework-skyrmionic-7fd4",
  "summary": "Four preprints from late November 2026 link knotted polarization, terahertz toroidal pulses and entanglement-like coherence through spatiotemporal metasurface control.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is spatiotemporal structure treated as a programmable degree of freedom in classical electromagnetic fields, with polarization as the main carrier. One preprint constructs vectorial wavepackets whose Stokes trajectories are linked or knotted. Another generates and tunes toroidal terahertz pulses with transient vectorial photocurrents in a graphene optoelectronic metasurface. Two space-time metasurface works program coherence: one synthesizes polarization states into quantum-inspired bits across 48 resolved channels, and the other realizes Bell- and GHZ-like multipartite states. The terahertz work shares the topological theme but uses a different generation route. What is new is the shift from static polarization topology toward joint control of topology, coherence and temporal structure within classical light.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-28"
}
